AI - Agent Infrastructure
=========================

A minimal runtime for non-interactive agents.

    ai [--help] AGENT [PROMPT...]

AGENT is a directory containing configuration, instructions, and tools.

PROMPT... is used as prompt text. If stdin is not a terminal, it is appended to
the prompt.

Writes a JSONL transcript to stdout.


Agents
------

An agent is a directory containing:

config.json:

  {
     "model": <name>
     "api": "anthropic-messages" or "anthropic-vertex" or
            "google-generate-content" or "openai-responses",
     "baseURL": <base URL of the API>,
     "credentialName": <name of environment variable containing API key>
  }

  If "api", "baseURL", or "credentialName" are not given, they are inferred
  from "model".

instructions.md

  High priority instructions for the agent.

tools/

  A directory of executables that are exposed to the model as tools
  (non-executable files and directories are ignored). Each of them must output
  its schema when invoked with "--tool":

    {
      "name": <name>,
      "description": <description>,
      "arguments": [ { "name": <name>, "description": <description> } ] or
                   { "name": <name>, "description": <description> }
    }

  The array form of "arguments" exposes each argument as a named string and
  passes them as positional command line arguments to the tool. The object form
  exposes a single array of strings.

  Tools stdout is returned verbatim to the model and stderr is only visible in
  the transcript. If a tool fails, the whole agent run is aborted.

  Tools run as trusted programs in the directory where "ai" was started and
  inherit its environment. Each tool is responsible for its own containment
  policy.


Transcripts
-----------

During operation, ai outputs JSONL events:

  {
    "type": "start",
    "timestamp": <ISO 8601 timestamp>,
    "payload": {
      "agent": {
        "model": <model configuration from config.json>,
        "instructions": <contents of instructions.md>,
        "tools": { <name>: <schema> }
      },
      "prompt": [ <user messages> ]
    }
  }

  {
    "type": "model",
    "timestamp": <ISO 8601 timestamp>,
    "payload": {
      "message": <message from the model>
    }
  }

  {
    "type": "toolCall",
    "timestamp": <ISO 8601 timestamp>,
    "payload": {
      "id": <id>,
      "tool": <tool name>,
      "arguments": { <argument name>: <argument value> }
    }
  }

  {
    "type": "toolResult",
    "timestamp": <ISO 8601 timestamp>,
    "payload": {
      "id": <id>,
      "result": <tool output>
    }
  }

  {
    "type": "end",
    "timestamp": <ISO 8601 timestamp>,
    "payload": {}
  }
